  story: "Mike Frehner and his wife Crystal have run Hottie Hair, a family salon and extensions business in Las Vegas, since 2006; it now has three locations. Frehner is also a software engineer. He rebuilt the company's website and booking flow with AI coding help (Claude), then added e-commerce-style abandoned-cart recovery for unfinished appointments — something he says most salons still lack. The system runs on its own; stylists and the front desk do not do outreach. Crystal worried for months that the follow-ups were just bugging people. In May he sat her down with the dashboard.",
  results: ["16% of abandoned bookings came back through the email flow (per Frehner's first-hand Medium post).", "17.3% once text messages were added.", "Tracked recovered bookings had crossed $10,000 when he showed Crystal the numbers.", "Note: Frehner does not say over what period the $10,000 was recovered or how many bookings were abandoned."],
