  start: ["Measure how many visitors start a booking vs. how many finish, so you know what you are losing.", "If you cannot build software yourself, ask your booking vendor whether they offer abandoned-booking email or text follow-up; Frehner built his own with Claude because salon SaaS often does not.", "Only message people who left contact details and consented, and include an easy opt-out.", "Make the first message specific: name the service and stylist they chose, not a generic \"come back.\"", "Stop the sequence the moment they book or opt out, and review recovery rates with a co-founder who protects the client experience."],
