  business: "Homely Stay (Germany; founder Nicole Gödecke)", type: "rentals",
  job: "An AI answers routine guest questions within seconds across Airbnb, Booking.com and WhatsApp, while if-this-then-that automations release check-in instructions only after a guest completes verification, work out city tax by guest type, and sell early check-in, late checkout and extras as paid add-ons.",
  story: "Homely Stay is a full-service vacation rental management company with 27 listings spread over a 300-kilometre area in Germany, run by a team of one and a half. Founder Nicole Gödecke previously managed operations for an 800-unit portfolio. Before switching, guests got separate links from different tools for registration and city tax, the digital guidebook and Stripe payments for add-ons, and her property management system could not hold back a message until a guest had registered or paid. Every morning before arrivals she pulled information from several systems by hand to check who had registered, who had paid and who might be a risk. She moved guest messaging, registration, city tax, check-in, guidebooks and add-on sales into Enso Connect, keeping Hostaway as her property management system and Chekin for authority reporting. She has used Enso Connect since she had 12 apartments.",
  results: ["73% of guest messages are automated (per the Enso Connect case study).", "\"Three seconds after I get a guest message, EnsoAI has already answered, and the answer is spot on,\" Gödecke says in the case study.", "Guests arriving in the middle of the night can check themselves in once they finish registering, even with her phone off.", "Early check-in and late checkout, which used to be absorbed for free, are now paid add-ons; a baby cot costs 10 euros per stay.", "Enso Connect replaced five separate tools, according to the case study."],
  tools: ["Enso Connect (EnsoAI guest messaging and guest portal)", "Hostaway (property management system)", "Chekin (guest registration reporting)"],
