  added: "2026-10-22",
  title: "A vegan cheese maker used Claude to dig through a year of shipping invoices and claw back overcharges from its carrier",
  business: "Rebel Cheese (Austin, Texas; co-founder Kirsten Maitland)", type: "makers",
  job: "Reads a year of carrier invoices against the shipping contract to find overcharge patterns, then checks each new week's invoices for charges that don't match the contract so the team can claim credits.",
  story: "Rebel Cheese ships tens of thousands of orders of perishable, handcrafted vegan cheese across the US, and the holiday season is its busiest time. \"Q4 is all hands, heads down, get it out the door, make sure customers are happy,\" co-founder Kirsten Maitland wrote. \"There's no time to stop and analyze anything.\" After its best holiday season ever, the bank account didn't reflect it, and she discovered the company had paid $250,000 more for shipping than planned. Hiring people to dig into it wasn't an option, so she turned to Anthropic's Claude. The carrier's invoices run hundreds of pages a week, with fees layered inside fees. She then used Claude together with Manus to build a small tool that keeps checking invoices against the contract.",
  results: ["\"I handed it a year of invoices and a contract, and it found patterns I would have needed a forensic accountant to surface, which would have been time-consuming and expensive,\" Maitland told Fast Company.", "Rebel Cheese used the AI tools to claw back overcharges from the carrier, according to Fast Company. The $250,000 figure is what the company paid for shipping above plan, not the amount recovered."],
