  title: "A spice-shop owner uses Gemini to sort a flood of inquiries, personalize replies and mock up flyers and events",
  business: "The Spice Suite (Washington, D.C.; founder Angel Gregorio)", type: "shops",
  job: "Summarizes the emails and sponsorship inquiries that arrive all day, helps the small team reply in a way that feels personal, makes quick assets like farmers-market flyers, and turns the owner's event ideas into images she can share.",
  story: "Angel Gregorio opened The Spice Suite in Washington, D.C. eleven years ago, then redeveloped a vacant auto body shop into Black and Forth, a strip mall where women run pop-up businesses from shipping containers, with a Sunday farmers market and free business classes. Her small team was juggling email and sponsorship inquiries 'all day, every day', so they started using Google Gemini to summarize inquiries, draft personalized replies and make flyers. For an event at the Spice Suite marking America's 250th anniversary, she described the look she wanted (a bonfire, but upscale, like a cookout) and Gemini generated an image she could hand to her PR person.",
  results: ["\"It's increased my capacity to do more things. Stuff I would have put off for when I had a lot of time, like designing a product, imagining what an event could look like, I can now do in between tasks,\" Angel says.", "\"As a business owner without a Chief Financial Officer or Chief Operating Officer, it's just me at the top, so I turn to Gemini all the time for ideating.\"", "Note: this interview was published by Google, the vendor. It gives no time or dollar figures."],
