  story: "321 Coffee runs cafés and a roasting facility in Raleigh and was founded to provide meaningful employment for people with intellectual and developmental disabilities. Its small founding team (Lindsay, Michael and Mallory) wears every hat, from operations to marketing and shipping logistics. Lenovo, which has worked with the business since 2021, moved it onto Microsoft 365, supplied AI PCs and Microsoft 365 and Copilot licenses, and ran tailored Copilot training sessions built around the team's own pain points, followed by a Q&A a few weeks later.",
  results: ["Through the trainings, the team was able to save up to 30 hours a week (per the source).", "Lindsay: \"I used to spend anywhere from 30 minutes to an hour writing LinkedIn posts, now I can write a post in as quickly as 5 minutes.\"", "Michael pulls shipping codes in seconds, a process that previously took 2 hours.", "Mallory nicknamed Copilot her \"intern\" because it drafts social copy and cuts repetitive admin.", "Note: this is a Lenovo press release. Lenovo supplied the hardware, Microsoft 365 and Copilot licenses, migration help and training; the source does not say what this would cost a business on its own."],
