  business: "Jennifer Beadles (rental portfolio across several US states, including Washington and Idaho)", type: "rentals",
  job: "A bilingual (English and Spanish) voice AI agent answers every rental inquiry call around the clock, answers questions about the unit, offers a showing and texts a pre-application; follow-up emails and texts chase anyone who stalls; AI virtual staging furnishes iPhone photos of vacant units.",
  story: "Jennifer Beadles was paying property managers a percentage of rent and still chasing them about vacant units, billing mistakes and slow maintenance, so she fired two of them. She replaced them with one full-time remote operations hire and a three-part AI leasing setup. Her rule for the staging prompt is strict: add furniture without changing any hard surfaces, fixtures, flooring, windows or walls. She also uploads listings to Zillow by hand so inquiries land in her own inbox and flow into the same automated follow-up.",
  results: ["Adding AI-staged furniture to listing photos increased showings by 50 percent in her own test.", "She says the system gets units leased in under a week, and one unit leased in a single day.", "An investor who copied the setup in Chattanooga, Tennessee saw the agent handle 64 calls entirely in Spanish.", "Together with the remote hire, the change has produced $11,600 a year in savings and new revenue; most of that ($5,000 insurance savings, $6,600 more rent) is credited to the remote operator, not the AI.", "Her caution: with only one or two units the remote-hire math doesn't work yet, and self-management with a basic automation stack is the better step. Note: the voice AI vendor isn't named, and no AI cost or setup time is given."],
  tools: ["Voice AI phone agent (vendor not named)", "Automated email and SMS follow-up in the same platform", "RentStager (AI virtual staging)", "Zillow"],
  cost: null,
  setupTime: null,
  start: ["Send every rental inquiry call to a voice AI agent trained on that listing's details, so 2 a.m. callers get an answer instead of voicemail.", "Have it text a pre-application, and only offer showing times once the application is in.", "Set automatic follow-ups for each stall point: called but didn't apply, applied but didn't book, booked a showing.", "Stage vacant-unit photos with AI, but tell it never to change floors, fixtures, windows or walls, so the listing stays honest."],
  sourceName: "Addicted to ROI (Jennifer Beadles): How I replaced two property managers with one remote hire and an AI leasing system (Feb 2026)",
